# What never needs to reach the build context.
#
# The context is the repo root (see `deploy/Dockerfile`), and every byte of it is
# sent to the daemon before the first instruction runs. That transfer is inside
# S8's five-minute cold-start budget, so this file is a performance control
# rather than housekeeping — `.git/` alone is usually larger than the source.
#
# It is also a safety control: `.env` holds a real provider credential, and
# without the rule below a `COPY . .` in any future edit of the Dockerfile would
# bake it into a layer. The Dockerfile copies named paths today; this makes that
# a defence in depth rather than the only thing standing between a key and an
# image.

# Credentials. `.env.example` is committed and carries no secret; `.env` does.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Version control and CI
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Not used at runtime. Tests run on the host (NFR-2 — no network, no Redis), and
# the compose stack is not a test dependency.
tests/
docs/
scripts/
measurements/

# The compose stack itself, and the provisioning the other services bind-mount
# rather than the gateway image carrying. `deploy/keel.demo.yaml` IS copied — it
# is named explicitly in the Dockerfile, and an ignore rule here would break that
# COPY, so the directory is not excluded wholesale.
docker-compose.yml
deploy/prometheus/
deploy/grafana/

# Tooling caches and build artefacts
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# Environments — a local .venv can be hundreds of megabytes and is never useful
# inside the image.
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Editors and OS
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
